### star-code-reviewer/SKILL.md
--- 1
2. **Find wide, verify before reporting.** When available, use read-only `star_subagent` collectors (`subagent_type: Explore`, `model:` the READ tier value, omitted when empty) from a context not party to the code under review, and size the fan-out to the scope. Every delegate follows `references/review_rubric.md`, never writes, and never grades the overall verdict. Independent review remains the goal; if `star_subagent` is unavailable, perform one local pass, record that limitation, and do not repeatedly ask for unavailable tooling. Re-read the cited code for every blocker/major finding before it enters the report; downgrade or drop what does not hold up.
+++ 1
2. **Find wide, verify before reporting.** When available, call `star_subagent` with `agent: "star-collector"` and the READ-tier `model` when non-empty, from a context not party to the code under review; size the fan-out to the scope. Every delegate follows `references/review_rubric.md`, never writes, and never grades the overall verdict. If `star_subagent` is unavailable, perform one local pass, record that limitation, and do not repeatedly ask for unavailable tooling. Re-read every blocker/major citation before reporting it.
### star-code-reviewer/SKILL.md
--- 1
- **How many is the main agent's call**, sized to the work (conventions §6.2): read-only `star_subagent` subagents (`subagent_type: Explore`, `model:` the READ tier value, omitted when empty) run in parallel, each given the rubric, the review rule digest built at Step 1 — the same block, verbatim, for all of them — and its exact file list, returning the structured finding format in `references/review_rubric.md`. Collectors never write, never review outside their file list, never grade the overall verdict. One collector can carry a coherent scope up to roughly 50 files; past that, partition package by package in groups of 10–15, so a 60-file tree goes to four or five collectors rather than sixty. A package that hangs together may run longer instead of being cut only to hit a group size.
+++ 1
- **How many is the main agent's call**, sized to the work (conventions §6.2): parallel `star_subagent` calls with `agent: "star-collector"` and the READ-tier `model` when non-empty, each given the rubric, shared rule digest, and exact file list. Collectors never write, exceed their list, or grade the verdict. One can carry a coherent scope up to roughly 50 files; larger scopes partition package by package in groups of 10–15.
